.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt DLOPEN 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm dlopen
.Nm dlsym
.Nm dlerror
.Nm dl_iterate_phdr
.Nd dynamic loading
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dlfcn.h
.Ft void *
.Fn dlopen "const char *path" "int mode"
.Ft void *
.Fn dlsym "void *handle" "const char *symbol"
.Ft char *
.Fn dlerror void
.Ft int
.Fn dl_iterate_phdr "int (*callback)(struct dl_phdr_info *, size_t, void *)" "void *data"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The dynamic-loader interface opens a shared object, resolves a symbol, reports the last error
and walks the loaded objects.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dlopen and .Fn dlsym return a handle or symbol address, or a null pointer. .Fn dlerror
returns a message or a null pointer. .Fn dl_iterate_phdr returns the callback result.
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn dlerror returns a human-readable message; the loader does not set errno for these calls.
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024 and the ELF extension; ring 1.
.Sh CAVEATS
The loader uses no hints file, libc.so.1 is the only DT_NEEDED dependency and
RTLD_DEEPBIND is not supported. See C62 and document 13.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dlopen 3
.Xr ld-elf.so.1 8
.Xr libc 7
